1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,654
MARK: Oh, come on. You've been sitting on that all night?

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,782
JASON: Thought you said I was easy to read.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,961
MARK: You are. When I'm sober.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,781
MARK: All right... you won. I'll send the coordinates.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:23,025
MARK: Jason. Look at me. Don't go there. I'm serious.

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:25,176
JASON: What happened out there?

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,481
MARK: I don't want to talk about it. Not tonight.

8
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:37,156
MARK: I think I'm done, Jason. I just... don't have it in me anymore. I used to love this work.

9
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:43,906
JASON: I'm tired of scraping by. One good haul, and Stacy and I might actually get somewhere.

10
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,357
MARK: Yeah... I used to tell myself that too.

11
00:00:50,510 --> 00:00:53,475
MARK: Wait... you're going anyway, aren't you? I know you.

12
00:00:56,510 --> 00:01:02,404
MARK: My pack's still out there. Little shelter, east of the yard road. Broken amber marker by the drain.

13
00:01:04,510 --> 00:01:05,737
JASON: You left your gear?

14
00:01:07,510 --> 00:01:12,222
MARK: There's a computer in there. Looks like junk. It isn't. I'll send you the software.

15
00:01:15,510 --> 00:01:20,850
MARK: Take it. I'm not going back. But listen... if it feels wrong, you leave. Right away.
